{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792691951,"nonce":"p383mGS1y2q2Zfr8j3n5ZxqrWgw=","title":"Render raw RGBA images through native path clips","message":"Child of 369499d9d754d8353823d4eb9ff5ff76e5469007b2983e58b3a677f88b5bbc6c.\n\nClipShape::Path is currently ignored by raw-image emission, including rectangular scissors when a path is the selected clip. Support raw-image path clips through the existing self-contained image clip payload. Capture the path's complete affine and pending fill rule at push_clip, flatten curves in physical screen space, close filled subpaths and separate contours. Preserve those rows through batch drains, foreground extraction, motion/scratch ownership, tight targets and cache replay.\n\nThis bounded slice covers draw_rgba_pixels. SDF/path/text primitive support for native path clips, arbitrary clip-stack intersections, and shared ClipPath/CSS enum changes remain outside it. Verify independent offscreen pixels, malformed/empty path behavior, CPU ownership invariants, all native storage modes and the complete required gate. No pushes.","files":null}]}